From a807c46758a180d0124c32dfb2888827548fa23a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:08:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(v2): deliver session events only to the folder that owns
 the session tree

OpenCode V2 runs one plugin instance per warm folder and hands each of them the
whole process's event stream: the plugin context carries no Location, so the
bus does not scope plugin subscriptions. V1 hooks assume a host-scoped stream.
With 12 warm folders, one probe session's session.error made 12 runtime-fallback
retries into the same session (12 agent switches, a model switch, 12 copies of
the prompt), each instance applying its own folder's config.

The V2 hook bridge now checks ownership before shaping an event for the V1
hooks: an instance owns a session when the session tree's root lives in its
folder (one owner per tree; a child delegate-task moved elsewhere stays with
the folder that created it). The folder comes from the session's own record
(session.get, 2 s timeout, cached per session), never from the event envelope,
which carries the publisher's location. Events without a session pass;
unresolvable sessions fail open and are not cached.

Tests (host.test.ts): two folders sharing one stream, one failed session ->
exactly one retry and no model switch in the foreign folder (old: 2 prompts);
foreign session events filtered; moved child owned by its root's folder;
fail-open without caching; one lookup per session; non-session events pass.
